# a schema is a taxonomy loaded after the fact. it says which kinds are shown
# under one name, so naming a thing is one word instead of seventeen. it
# changes no line and no column already built — only what the menu offers and
# what a column built from a drawer is called.
schema triage
# on its own it draws what is in force. a drawer carries the count of values it
# reaches, because that is the one thing about it you cannot read off its name;
# a leaf carries its name, because its count is one add away.
schema
# 78 kinds become 14 names. the counts are unions at every level and never
# sums: text-shape reads 301 where its fifteen kinds add up to about 670, and
# the gap is the strings that are a word and a string and a short-string at
# once.
add
# a drawer is added, narrowed and typed exactly like a kind. more than one way
# in, so it says what it would merge and waits — which is also how you look
# inside one without taking it.
add network
add network
# the same offers as one step at a time, rolled up. 43 of the 45 values can
# step to something that lands back inside network, and the exits worth seeing
# are the 19 into text and the 2 into identity.
add
# the same column under a network engineer's schema. same rows, same steps,
# different vocabulary: triage says you are inside the network world, netops
# says where inside. addresses reads 21, exactly what ip reads alone, so
# internal-ip and valid-ip reach nothing ip does not — the pile agreeing with
# what the schema claimed was narrower.
schema netops
add
# and with nothing in force, the 23 kinds that were there the whole time. the
# column keeps the name it was built with, because a schema never revises a
# reading already made.
schema off
add
# a schema does not have to match the pile. six of the gardener's members are
# not kinds anybody here wrote, so they read zero and it says which.
schema gardener
